Hello everyone,

This morning several staff received emails that look like they come from
Kestrel Payroll, asking you to "confirm your direct deposit" before the
November 20 pay run. These emails are not from Kestrel.

- Kestrel never asks for banking details by email. Direct deposit changes
  are made only through HR.
- Genuine Kestrel emails come from kestrelpay.example. Check the address
  carefully: the fake ones use a lookalike.
- Don't click links in payroll emails. Reach Kestrel through the link on
  the intranet's HR page instead.

If you received one, use the Report Phish button in your mail client and
delete it. If you clicked or entered any details, call the Service Desk
at ext. 4357 right away. You won't be in trouble - reporting quickly is
what lets us protect your pay.

DevTalk IT Security

